cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'AIDE-SAI: a modular dycore-aerosol-radiation coupler for stratospheric aerosol injection'
abstract: >-
  A GPU (JAX) coupler for stratospheric aerosol injection in which each
  physical process - meteorology (the dycore), boundary climatology,
  transport, aerosol microphysics, settling and radiation - sits in a
  swappable slot filled by a numerical scheme or, in future, a learned
  emulator. A
  linking, i.e. which scheme fills each slot and which pinned submodule commit
  provides it, is a preset file. Two numerical linkings ship: prescribed
  CESM2 meteorology on the f09 grid, and jcm-strat meteorology on its T63
  Gaussian grid, each with a monthly CESM boundary climatology, 40-bin TOMAS
  sectional microphysics (tomas_jax.fast) for SO2, H2SO4 and sulfate aerosol
  with continuous SO2 injection, SO2-OH chemistry, nucleation, condensation
  and coagulation, gravitational settling of the wet H2SO4/H2O droplet through
  an open band bottom, semi-Lagrangian transport, and RRTMGP radiative
  transfer with Mie optics. The meteorology is prescribed, so the circulation
  does not respond to the aerosol.
